{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm","id":1225892,"title":"Dragon-Bloods: Request a Charm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-08T09:09:32-07:00","id":1225892,"title":"Dragon-Bloods: Request a Charm","content":"I'd like to get back into writing Charms. <br /> <br /> Give an outline of a Charm you would like for WFHW, as specific or vague as you like, and I will do my best to respond to as many as I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T09:42:16-07:00","id":1225903,"title":"","content":"Swornkinship charm, it helps your heartmates in presence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13712,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","user":"Illaden","date":". 06-08-2018, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T09:52:42-07:00","id":1225906,"title":"","content":"Brawl charm about using enemies as improvised weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T10:00:59-07:00","id":1225908,"title":"","content":"An Air-aspected melee charm that supplements an attack or enhances a parry and <i>isn't </i>a way to extend the range of your attack, make multiple attacks, or disarm/root people by freezing them into place (I can write those myself).<br /> <br /> Basically, surprise me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T10:06:59-07:00","id":1225910,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea I had that started as &quot;Glorious Terrestrial BLEH&quot; but actually turned into... like an idea. Here is my rough outline.<br /> <br /> Abrupt Interjection of Distaste Method (Fire, Socialize)<br /> Upon hearing social influence (and recognizing it as such, which might require rolls or something if the influence is shrouded by magic? I'unno) directed at another character in the scene which is blatantly antithetical to one of her Intimacies, the Exalt may use this Charm to interject. This applies a dice penalty to the social influence roll equal to the value (positive or negative? unsure!) of the Intimacy. If this causes the social influence to fail, the character who attempted the influence retains the penalty if he attempts to make the same influence roll on another target in the scene (i.e. if the Exalt stopped a merchant from trying to convince an official to interpret a law in his favor, the merchant gets the same penalty if in the same scene he tries to convince a different official to do the same thing). He may spend 1 Willpower to resist this effect.<br /> This Charm may be used once per scene unless reset by causing a non-trivial character in the scene to hold the same Intimacy she used to activate the Charm, at the same intensity. Even after resetting, this Charm may not be used with the same Intimacy in the same scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T10:14:33-07:00","id":1225911,"title":"","content":"An Occult Charm (or two Charms to tier the effects perhaps) to tame unbound Elementals by invoking the authority of the appropriate Dragon. I\u2019m imagining it initially only working with the DB\u2019s Aspect elementals, with purchasable upgrades for the other elements - but if you make the charm weaker it could just count as situationally aligned with whatever element the elemental is.<br /> <br /> If you do separate Charms I was thinking the lower essence one is just a \u201cdon\u2019t attack\u201d one, with the more powerful one being an upgrade making it able to command actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T10:34:33-07:00","id":1225920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm#post1225892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to get back into writing Charms.<br /> <br /> Give an outline of a Charm you would like for WFHW, as specific or vague as you like, and I will do my best to respond to as many as I can.</div> </div> </div> </div>An upgrade to Rebirth of Ivy and Flesh, or any two Medicine Charms, which allows for the restoration of lost limbs/fingers/eyes/Crippling Wounds, rather than just repairing tissues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T11:59:47-07:00","id":1225941,"title":"","content":"An Earth Sail charm that does something like anchor a ship with the weight of Earth or raises up spires of Earth from the deeps to create a hazard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T12:18:54-07:00","id":1225944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225920#post1225920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An upgrade to Rebirth of Ivy and Flesh, or any two Medicine Charms, which allows for the restoration of lost limbs/fingers/eyes/Crippling Wounds, rather than just repairing tissues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of true restoration of limbs, how about prosthetics made of an element (Plant matter is the most obvious, but Ming Hua Style Water tendrils are always cool!)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-08-2018, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T12:35:15-07:00","id":1225951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225944#post1225944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Instead of true restoration of limbs, how about prosthetics made of an element (Plant matter is the most obvious, but Ming Hua Style Water tendrils are always cool!)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I meant; there's a character idea on Ask the Devs: pg. 778 that comes to mind, in particular.<br /> The point being, the Dragonblooded might not be able to replicate the perfection of Solar Medicine, perhaps, but manifesting a suitable Wood-Dragon clawed foot, an eye made of fire, or a Stone-Jade Fist as prosthetics would be very good.<br /> Otherwise, I'd definitely pursue visually-similar Artifact prosthetics, should GMs imagine healing a Crippling Wound the player chose to imflict upon themselves in combat 'cheap'. Rebirth of Ivy and Flesh is already Perilous, with a cooldown measured in a full story or the healing of an Incapacitated box; how much more might re required to return a whole limb, even in a visiblly-Elemental form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T14:32:43-07:00","id":1225972,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a water-melee Charm that facilitates your weapon flowing around a parry... but I have no idea how to balance that without pulling the 2E bullshit of making your charm fail against a potent opponent you might actually need it against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-08T14:43:33-07:00","id":1225974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225972#post1225972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea for a water-melee Charm that facilitates your weapon flowing around a parry... but I have no idea how to balance that without pulling the 2E bullshit of making your charm fail against a potent opponent you might actually need it against.</div> </div> </div> </div>The capstone of Single Point seems like a good place to start from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T05:27:13-07:00","id":1226051,"title":"","content":"How about a Water World type charm? Flood the area with immense amounts of water, bring the ocean on land and swim towards the sky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24306-spear37","name":"Spear37","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-09T12:27:19-07:00","id":1226111,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I've made a few, more later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225903#post1225903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swornkinship charm, it helps your heartmates in presence</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All For One</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 2m, 4i; Mins:War 4, Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:Earth, Balanced</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:Until next turn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms:Tactics Mean Everything</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Focusing her will upon an opponent\u2019s defeat, the Dragon-Blood leads her allies in striking him down. After making an attack on an enemy or commanding a battle group to do so, the Exalt can activate this Charm. Up to four selected allies or battle groups who attack the same opponent before the Dragon-Blood\u2019s next turn gain bonus dice on their attempt, one for the first, two for the second and so on. Sworn Kin gain this bonus as non-Charm dice. Multiple uses of this Charm do not stack.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dancing Firefly Inspiration</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m; Mins:Presence 4, Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:Fire, Balanced</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:Until next turn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms:Glowing Coal Radiance</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The rage of flame can be terrifying, but no less is its passion inspiring. The Dragon-Blood exhorts an ally to press themselves beyond their limits, bolstering their will to excel. An ally who can hear the Dragon-Blood gains a bonus point of Willpower, which can exceed his normal Willpower pool. This bonus Willpower point can be used for any purpose except as part of the cost of a Charm activation, but it is wasted if it is not used by the time the Charm ends. The Dragon-Blood can target (Essence/2) of her Sworn Kin with this Charm rather than a single target, granting the benefit to each. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Fire Aura, this Simple Charm can be placed in a flurry with other social actions. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Soul-Phalanx Methodology</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: (+3m); Mins:Integrity 5, Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:Earth</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms:Flawless Diamond Heart</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When faced by influence made against the Dragon-Blood and one or more of her Sworn Kin, the Exalt may activate Flawless Diamond Heart at an increased cost of 10m to extend its benefits to all affected members of the Hearth. Hearthmates must use a shared or otherwise complimentary intimacy to the one the Dragon-Blood uses, which must be held at the major or defining level. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TDS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225906#post1225906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brawl charm about using enemies as improvised weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cast Upon the Rocks</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m, 1wp, 2 rounds of control; Mins:Brawl 4, Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:Withering-only, Water</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms:Water Dragon\u2019s Coils, Inescapable Whirlpool Hold</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The merciless current of the Dragon-Blood\u2019s motion crushes her foe against the banks of his own allies. The Exalt can use this Charm to end a grapple by performing a slam attack. She does so by striking another nearby opponent with her grappled foe\u2019s body, constituting a separate withering attack against the second opponent with an improvised weapon. Human sized opponents are generally considered heavy mundane weapons, but the Storyteller should modify the weapon profile as appropriate. Once per scene unless reset by dealing damage with a decisive savaging or slam attack in a grapple.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Water Aura, Cast Upon the Rocks can generate a withering savage attack instead of a slam. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225908#post1225908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Air-aspected melee charm that supplements an attack or enhances a parry and <i>isn't </i>a way to extend the range of your attack, make multiple attacks, or disarm/root people by freezing them into place (I can write those myself).</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225908#post1225908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Basically, surprise me.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cyclone-Blade Slash</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 3m, expend Air Aura; Mins:Melee 5, Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:Air, Aura, Uniform</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms:Crossfire Flash</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Grasping the speed of the wind itself, the Dragon-Blood steps between raindrops and delivers a blow faster than the eye can follow. Outside of the normal turn order, she selects a target currently at short range, moves towards him and makes a single Melee attack. This counts as her action for the round. This Charm can be used once per scene, unless the Dragon-Blood resets to base after a decisive attack and then regains enough Initiative to act before all opponents on her turn. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Razor Wind Mantle</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:Air</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:Until next turn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms:Flame-Borne Interception, Graceful Flowing Defense</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chill winds rise in the Dragon-Blood\u2019s wake, forming pellucid blades of Essence to strike away attacks that would harm her. She assumes a Full Defence, paying the cost of this Charm in place of the normal Initiative cost. She ignores up to (Melee) points of onslaught penalty, instead gaining a point of Initiative whenever she successfully parries an attack. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In Air Aura, the cost of this Charm is reduced to 3m if it is activated simultaneously with Flame-Borne Interception, for a total of 6m. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cold Winter Vengeance Stance</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m; Mins:Melee 4, Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:Air, Decisive-only</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms:Razor Wind Mantle</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">After spending at least one turn in combat during which she did not make an attack, a decisive attack enhanced with this Charm doubles 10s on the damage roll and adds additional damage dice from threshold successes on the attack roll, to a maximum of the onslaught penalty she shed at the beginning of her round. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dance of the Thunder Dragon</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m; Mins:Melee 5, Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type:Reflexive</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords:Air, Aura, Withering-only, Counterattack</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration:Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms:Blinding Spark Distraction, Razor Wind Mantle</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The flash of lightning presages the fury of the storm. After successfully blinding her attacker with Blinding Spark Distraction, the Dragon-Blood can launch an immediate withering counterattack against him.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-10-2018, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T05:15:07-07:00","id":1226431,"title":"","content":"Here are a few more, feedback is welcome, as are more requests.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225910#post1225910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea I had that started as &quot;Glorious Terrestrial BLEH&quot; but actually turned into... like an idea. Here is my rough outline.<br /> <br /> Abrupt Interjection of Distaste Method (Fire, Socialize)<br /> Upon hearing social influence (and recognizing it as such, which might require rolls or something if the influence is shrouded by magic? I'unno) directed at another character in the scene which is blatantly antithetical to one of her Intimacies, the Exalt may use this Charm to interject. This applies a dice penalty to the social influence roll equal to the value (positive or negative? unsure!) of the Intimacy. If this causes the social influence to fail, the character who attempted the influence retains the penalty if he attempts to make the same influence roll on another target in the scene (i.e. if the Exalt stopped a merchant from trying to convince an official to interpret a law in his favor, the merchant gets the same penalty if in the same scene he tries to convince a different official to do the same thing). He may spend 1 Willpower to resist this effect.<br /> This Charm may be used once per scene unless reset by causing a non-trivial character in the scene to hold the same Intimacy she used to activate the Charm, at the same intensity. Even after resetting, this Charm may not be used with the same Intimacy in the same scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>We talked a little about this one on Discord, the original brief is a little too similar to existing Charms so I made an alternative that hopefully lives up to the spirit of the original while still being a useful addition to the set.<br /> <br /> <b>Scorching Brand of Reproach</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1wp; Mins:Presence 5, Essence 3<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords:Fire<br /> Duration:One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Loyalty-Reading Meditation<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood lays bare her soul, and its radiance sears any who would gainsay her. She declares one of her emotional intimacies to all present, rolling ([Charisma or Appearance] + Presence) against the Resolve of all present, ignoring the penalty for group influence. Anyone whose Resolve is overcome suffers a penalty on any social influence that diminishes opinion of the target of the intimacy (if the intimacy is positive) or supports the target of the intimacy (if it is negative). For example, the Dragon-Blood could declare her love and admiration for her betrothed, for whom she had a major emotional tie, inflicting a -3 dice penalty on any influence that might diminish opinion of him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225911#post1225911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Occult Charm (or two Charms to tier the effects perhaps) to tame unbound Elementals by invoking the authority of the appropriate Dragon. I\u2019m imagining it initially only working with the DB\u2019s Aspect elementals, with purchasable upgrades for the other elements - but if you make the charm weaker it could just count as situationally aligned with whatever element the elemental is.<br /> <br /> If you do separate Charms I was thinking the lower essence one is just a \u201cdon\u2019t attack\u201d one, with the more powerful one being an upgrade making it able to command actions.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Five Forces Emissary Approach</b><br /> Cost: 4m; Mins:Occult 3, Essence 1<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords:Wood, Balanced<br /> Duration:One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Hidden Secrets Whisper<br /> <br /> Through the blood of the dragons, the elemental dominion of the Terrestrial Exalted extends to all Creation. While this Charm is active, elementals matching the Dragon-Blood\u2019s Aspect count as having a minor tie of Respect towards her, as they perceive her worldly authority. The Storyteller may choose to extend this benefit to other spirits with a strong elemental affinity, such as forest or volcano gods.<br /> <br /> With Occult 4+, Essence 2+, the benefits of this Charm can extend to other elements, provided the Dragon-Blood is in the appropriate Elemental Aura.<br /> <br /> <b>Pact of the Awakened World</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1wp; Mins:Occult 5, Essence 3<br /> Type:Supplemental<br /> Keywords:Wood, Balanced<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Five Forces Emissary Approach<br /> <br /> When making a persuade action on an elemental with an Essence no greater than her own with the benefit of the minor intimacy granted by Five Forces Emissary Approach, the Dragon-Blood can use Pact of the Awakened World to make the intimacy count as Defining for an instant. This influence is not a form of control or sorcerous binding, but represents the Dragon-Blood using her occult knowledge to have the spirit recognize her natural authority over lesser elemental spirits of Creation. This Charm can only be used once per season on a given spirit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225920#post1225920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An upgrade to Rebirth of Ivy and Flesh, or any two Medicine Charms, which allows for the restoration of lost limbs/fingers/eyes/Crippling Wounds, rather than just repairing tissues.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Spring of Life\u2019s Resurgence</b><br /> Cost: 12m, 1wp; Mins:Medicine 5, Essence 4<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords:Wood<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Rebirth of Flesh and Ivy, Grevious Wound Alteration Energy<br /> <br /> Such is the medical genius of the Dragon-Blooded that they can bring life to even the most broken body. Over twelve hours of intensive work, the Dragon-Blood labours to align the meridians of her patient\u2019s body and begin the process of regrowing an amputated limb or recovering from some other similarly extreme condition. Repairing severed spines, replacing blind eyes, restoring skin and muscle tissue to a severe burn victim, no physical injury is beyond the Dragon-Blood\u2019s powers to restore. Any such attempt requires an (Intelligence + Medicine) roll of at least Difficulty 5, followed by a course of medicines, meditation, physiotherapy and other restorative regimens under the Dragon-Blood\u2019s supervision for anything from a day to a month depending on the severity of the injury.<br /> <br /> At the conclusion of the treatment, the subject will have their body fully restored, though it will be somewhat different than it was before. Replacement body parts appear to be carved from wood or grown from plant fibre, and will shed sap rather than blood when cut. Despite this oddity, the gifts of this Charm are fully functional and identical in function to natural body parts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225941#post1225941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Earth Sail charm that does something like anchor a ship with the weight of Earth or raises up spires of Earth from the deeps to create a hazard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must admit I'm having trouble with this one. I can't figure out a useful effect that isn't already covered by the Sail set. Any more insight you can offer into what you're after?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1225972#post1225972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an idea for a water-melee Charm that facilitates your weapon flowing around a parry... but I have no idea how to balance that without pulling the 2E bullshit of making your charm fail against a potent opponent you might actually need it against.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Unstoppable Surge Technique</b><br /> Cost: 5m, 5i, expend Water Aura; Mins:Melee 5, Essence 3<br /> Type:Reflexive<br /> Keywords:Water, Aura, Decisive-Only<br /> Duration:Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Roaring River Slash<br /> <br /> In the instant that it appears the Dragon-Blood\u2019s attack has been foiled, a razor-sharp lash of water flows forth from the edge of her weapon, striking past her opponent\u2019s defences. After failing to strike an opponent with a decisive attack. The Dragon-Blood can activate this Charm to immediately make a second decisive attack with her opponent\u2019s Defence lowered by half the successes on her initial attack, rounded up. Once per scene, unless reset by incapacitating an opponent with a decisive attack that did not benefit from this Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T06:15:58-07:00","id":1226444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1226431#post1226431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must admit I'm having trouble with this one. I can't figure out a useful effect that isn't already covered by the Sail set. Any more insight you can offer into what you're after?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think generally using Earth to slow down another ship, either through making a hazard like rock spires shooting up around it or binding the ship to the sea floor or coast or such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T06:52:35-07:00","id":1226450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1225892-dragon-bloods-request-a-charm?p=1226431#post1226431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We talked a little about this one on Discord, the original brief is a little too similar to existing Charms so I made an alternative that hopefully lives up to the spirit of the original while still being a useful addition to the set.<br /> <br /> <b>Scorching Brand of Reproach</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1wp; Mins:Presence 5, Essence 3<br /> Type:Simple<br /> Keywords:Fire<br /> Duration:One scene<br /> Prerequisite Charms:Loyalty-Reading Meditation<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood lays bare her soul, and its radiance sears any who would gainsay her. She declares one of her emotional intimacies to all present, rolling ([Charisma or Appearance] + Presence) against the Resolve of all present, ignoring the penalty for group influence. Anyone whose Resolve is overcome suffers a penalty on any social influence that diminishes opinion of the target of the intimacy (if the intimacy is positive) or supports the target of the intimacy (if it is negative). For example, the Dragon-Blood could declare her love and admiration for her betrothed, for whom she had a major emotional tie, inflicting a -3 dice penalty on any influence that might diminish opinion of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is super cool and feels very Fire. Thanks!<br /> <br /> Also, all the other Charms are rad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 06-11-2018, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T07:32:12-07:00","id":1226453,"title":"","content":"A few ideas:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Wood Occult charm to somehow detect spirits by smelling them (maybe an alternative to spirit-sight, maybe a JB booster, maybe a way to detect spirits possessing hosts)</li> <li>Occult charm to become immaterial</li> <li>Fire Occult charm to inscribe or brand indelible, mystical symbols or writing into an object</li> <li>Occult charm to let you do something with Aura or Anima and elemental demesnes or manses</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T09:43:17-07:00","id":1226485,"title":"","content":"I really dig the air melee branch of charms. Got an air aspected Meleeist in my game right now who will definitely be able to benefit from a tree that includes a charm for once he's at bonfire and locked into Air aura. Plus adding defensive and counterpunching utility.<br /> <br /> Edit: and I totally forgot a charm idea to throw out. I had some idea for a war or sail charm about expanding your anima over a ship or unit and using it as a signalling and coordination thing to allies but can't for the life of me think how to mechanize that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","user":"Alpharius","date":". 06-11-2018, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T09:35:23-07:00","id":1226815,"title":"","content":"LOVE what you did with the Occult Charms to utilize Aura. I\u2019m inclined to treat the Charms as aspected toward the elementals being utilized toward instead of defaulting to Wood, but that\u2019s a minor quibble.<br /> <br /> The Water Melee Charm is pretty terrifying, but I suppose the Aura keyword and reset requirement keeps it in check. Well done!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T20:51:29-07:00","id":1227040,"title":"","content":"A Brawl Charm that allows a team of Dragon-Blooded to work together in a clinch, potentially grappling with an enemy of Legendary Size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato",